            <ArticleTitle>Occupational asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occupational asthma is defined as &quot;a disease of variable airflow limitations and/or airway hyper-responsiveness due to causes and conditions attributable to a particular occupational environment and not stimuli that are being encountered outside the workplace.&quot; An analysis of general population-based studies published up to 2007 showed that 17.6% of all adult-onset asthma is due to workplace exposures. In this article, Different aspects of occupational asthma are briefly reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
